ount that signs in, per site. Autofill: off, or the site's profile. Workflows that fire on a page visit are skipped where off; a site's macros run when its pages load, as his own run. Co-pilot answers with the site's agent, or without the page where the mesh is off. Guardian: no listeners, or no chat capture, where off. Resume state: the page keeps its place as he leaves and gets it back on a revisit, scroll and forms, never a password (src/rewind/resume.js) — rewind's snapshots could not, they are taken at load on agent navigations; said in the spec's addendum. Unset sites behave as before. test-site-readers 7/7. See CHANGELOG-0.60.216.md.] [James, 2026-10-23: "I need site specific settings for the autofill, macros, workflows, passwords/accounts, snowflake, resume state. Cleardriver, agentmesh and guardian setting. Also need a processes screen for background tabs and activity." SP1 of docs/2026-10-23-site-profile-processes-phasemap.spec: one table of per-site keys for every feature he named (clear-glass/src/site-settings/keys.js, defaults are today's behaviour) and one resolver, siteProfile(url) — the site's value, else the global option, else the default, each marked with where it came from — over the per-origin store Clear Glass already had; the Snowflake route per site is one netPolicy origin rule (site.<host>), checked on a copy first so a refused route keeps the one it had. IPC site-profile:*, /cli/site-profile, cg.siteProfile. No feature reads it yet (SP2), and there is no screen yet (SP3). Readings to confirm: "resume state" read as where he was on a site on a revisit; "snowflake" per site read as the site's route. test-site-profile 3/3. See CHANGELOG-0.60.215.md.] [James, with a screenshot of the ☰ menu's Tools: "also still here? why? supposed to be migrated". Agent Mesh, Element Picker and NCP Providers moved into Guardian's agents hub in 0.60.180 (shell/agents.js); 0.60.210's rebuilt Tools listed every unpinned tool and brought them back — the coder's mis