from new tab?" Zoom has been in Clear Glass's core since 0.60.183; what it lacked was a place on the toolbar — Zoom controls (− level +, the level resets to 100%) is now a pinnable built-in tool on the same core zoom as Ctrl +/−, the address bar's level and the ☰ menu's Zoom row. (0.60.210's zoom-plugin note came from the test fixture, not his install.) The start page's agents were not removed: the page read the list once and a failed early read stayed as "Guardian's provider host is not answering" — it now names what failed and reads the agents again every 3 s while open. test-browser-shell 28/28 (BST-22, BST-23 in Clear Glass). See CHANGELOG-0.60.211.md.] [James, 2026-10-22, with a screenshot of the ☰ menu: "customize toolbar and those toolbar links, and customize toolbar need to be rebuilt for  the new ui, they are cheap and crappy, and look bad." The tool rows and the pinned tool buttons drew text glyphs beside drawn icons. Each command now has a drawn icon and a line on what it does (src/toolbar/commands.js); the ☰ menu's Tools are the menu's own rows with a pin button and an Edit link; Customize toolbar is rebuilt on the shell's system — a live preview, two lists with each tool's icon and description, Pin / Unpin on every row, run-once actions as buttons. Found on the way: a plugin command with no button of its own was offered for pinning, which did nothing — it runs once now; Settings was listed twice. test-browser-shell 26/26 (BST-21 in Clear Glass). Also merged to main: 0.60.206–0.60.209 (HorrisEllis/Nexus#143). See CHANGELOG-0.60.210.md.] [0.60.209: James: "continue" — after Guardian, the next systems hold their own data. DL3 for six owners: versionium, ollama-bridge, architect, clear-glass, diagnostic and orchestrator resolve their data through lib/data-home.js; no code names their root data/ paths (test-data-rewired RW-01), Diagnostic's table — the registry's dataDir — points each at <folder>/data (RW-02), and at each one's boot its files come home (versionium 8, ollama 2, architect 1, clear-glass 1, diagnostic 5, orchestrator 5 in this tree). Their tables in cortex's store (SS2) follow per system; the order is corrected in the map's addendum. Found by running the tests one by one: ollama-command-index started ollama/server.js outside the sandbox, and its boot moved this checkout's real data/ollama files — the test now takes the sandbox, and data-home itself now sandboxes any test process before computing a path (as every resolver does); the clear-up's rollback rightly refused files the running server had appended to. The 68 tests that load these modules match 0.60.208 but one, test-agent-facts, whose check is now its intent (the cache never in the repo). See CHANGELOG-0.60.209.md.] [0.60.208: James: "start the data migration. look at the phases, any migrating data to the respective systems, and make each system responsible for it's own data." SS1, the first system end to end: Guardian. Its three requires of cortex's store are gone (data blockers 3 → 0): the callto agent keeps agent_calls, guardian_health, artifacts and toasts in Guardian's own store (agent_calls brought from cortex once, recorded) and sends event_log and cortex_memory through cortex's routes; bridge turns, flap events and flapping gaps go through cortex's POST /api/event and /api/gaps (buffered when cortex is down), and cortex keeps queue_uuid/comp_id top-level so the gap engine still matches them. DL3 for Guardian: every path resolves through lib/data-home.js — no code names data/guardian, so its files come home to guardian/data at its next boot; ledger-writer and cortex-write put a rewired system in its own folder and leave the rest. Found: guardian-job-persistence wrote real job files into the tree; it now asks the resolver (the sandbox). Not yet: data/ledger/guardian waits with every system's channel ledgers (15 code files name data/ledger). test-guardian-own-data 5/5; the 84 tests that load these modules match 0.60.207 except four that pinned